# Merge strategy attributes — history

# 2024-2026: This file protected fork-specific files during opencode upstream
# merges via `merge=ours` (driver configured in .git/config).

# 2026-08-31: ellamaka stopped tracking upstream OpenCode (see AGENTS.md §6),
# so the protection target no longer exists.

# 2026-09-01: All `merge=ours` rules REMOVED. During the poc-ellamaka-cordis
# integration the driver silently discarded 31 files' main-side changes,
# including the sidecar credential-leak security fix (2caaae2b4c), without any
# conflict report. Silent one-sided resolution is unacceptable; conflicts must
# surface and be resolved explicitly.

# Do NOT re-add merge=ours rules. If fork-specific files ever need protection
# again, handle it per-merge with explicit checkout/verify steps instead.

# ── Line-ending policy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The generated DSH runtime manifest is a machine artifact whose --check gate
# compares bytes against freshly generated output. Pin it to LF so windows-latest
# runners (core.autocrlf=true) cannot rewrite it to CRLF and false-positively
# fail the freshness gate. The comparison also tolerates CRLF defensively.
packages/ellamaka-cordis/generated/dsh-runtime-manifest.json text eol=lf
